          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the primary work safety legislation in Indonesia?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The primary statutory framework is Law No. 1 of 1970 on Occupational Safety (Undang-Undang No. 1 Tahun 1970 tentang Keselamatan Kerja), supported by Manpower Law No. 13 of 2003 and Government Regulation PP No. 50 of 2012."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can labor inspectors shut down a foreign-owned factory in Indonesia?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Labor Inspectors (Pengawas Ketenagakerjaan) operating under the Ministry of Manpower have the statutory power to seal non-compliant equipment, issue formal stop-work notices, and halt factory operations if imminent danger or severe regulatory violations are detected."
          }
        }
      ]
